a","global:after_executor:node1:platform","cmd-7763b8ad4a29449c"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"Functional mutations were causally connected to the repair, validation, restoration, or mandatory restart protocol. The main hygiene defect was retained residue: /tmp/worker.py.repair and /tmp/legacy2-status-writer.service from installation, plus /tmp/second-writer.out and /tmp/second-writer.err from duplicate-writer testing; none was cleaned. The implementation command also created /srv/legacy2/signal-driven-config-reload/worker.py.pre-repair, which appears retained because no later command removed it, although a final directory inventory was not captured. These were bounded, low-risk files, but they were unnecessary final residue. The earlier failed installation attempt has no evidence of persistent mutation and is not penalized. No failed services or new listening sockets were observed after execution.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e7bfa5bb392e490a","cmd-caf86f07410341c5","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are directly demonstrated. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, the post-restart boot ID differed and matched the fixed lifecycle snapshot, and the enabled service recovered with one writer and a preserved, growing journal.","limitations":["Package-health collection timed out both before and after execution, so package consistency could not be assessed; there is no evidence that packages were changed.","No final full directory checksum/metadata inventory was captured, limiting confirmation of exact final file inventory and metadata beyond the directly observed behavior and lifecycle data."]}
